          %h2#Idea Idea
          %p
            In a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \,\in\, C
            %strong pointed object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,x)
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+element"} global element
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            of the form
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \,\colon\, \ast \to X
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basepoint"} basepoint
          %p
            Pointed objects are distinguished from
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+objects"} inhabited objects
            in that the chosen point is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            rather than a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/property"} property
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of pointed objects is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            in the original category which preserves the basepoints. In other words, the category of pointed objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-slice+category"} co-slice category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast/C
            under the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
          %p#MoreGenerally
            (More generally, one might regard any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coslice+category"} coslice category
            under any object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \,\in\, C
            as the category of “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            \-pointed objects”. This is common in the case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = I
            is its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+unit"} tensor unit
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects+in+a+monoidal+category"} pointed objects in a monoidal category
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+element"} generalized element
          %p
            There is an obvious
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            which forgets the basepoint
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi C
                      %mtd
                        %mo ⟶
                      %mtd
                        %mi C
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtd
                        %mo ↦
                      %mtd
                        %mi X
                        %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{ccc}
                  \\ast/C &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; C
                  \\\
                  (X,x) &amp;\mapsto&amp; X
                  \\mathrlap{\,.}
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+colimit"} finite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint functor
            which takes an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to the coproduct
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast\sqcup X
            = succeed "\u201D)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maybe+monad"} maybe monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_+
            and called “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with a disjoint basepoint adjoined.” A pointed object is equivalently a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module+over+a+monad"} module over a monad
            for this monad.
          %h2#definition Definition
          #SliceCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{C}
              be an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %p
              The
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/X}
              is the category whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  objects are morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{A \\ \downarrow \\ X}
                  in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  morphisms are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting triangles
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi B
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                %mo ↘
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↙
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ A &amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp; B \\ &amp; {}_{}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow \\ &amp;&amp; X}
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %p
              Dually, the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coslice+category"} coslice category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{X/}
              is the category whose
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  objects are morphisms
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{X \\ \downarrow \\ A}
                  in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  morphisms are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting triangles
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↙
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ↘
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi A
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi B
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \array{ &amp;&amp; X \\ &amp; \swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow \\ A &amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp; B }
                  in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %p
              There is the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \;\colon \; \mathcal{C}_{/X}, \mathcal{C}^{X/} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}
            %p
              given by forgetting the morphisms to/from
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p We here focus on this class of examples:
          #CategoryOfPointedObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coslice+category"} coslice category
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SliceCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
              is the corresponding
              = succeed ":" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+pointed+objects"} category of pointed objects
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  objects are morphisms in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  of the form
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi x
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \overset{x}{\to} X
                  (hence an object
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  equipped with a choice of point; i.e. a
                  = succeed ");" do
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
              %li
                %p
                  morphisms are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting triangles
                  of the form
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo *
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mi x
                                %mo ↙
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo ↘
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mi y
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi f
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \&amp;&amp; \ast
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{x}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{y}}
                        \\\
                        X &amp;&amp; \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp; Y
                        }
                %p
                  (hence morphisms in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  which preserve the chosen points).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          #PointedSets.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The pointed objects in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+sets"} pointed sets
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Within the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/doctrine"} doctrine
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+categories"} cartesian monoidal categories
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal notions
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebraic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structures"} structures
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/units"} units
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+objects"} natural numbers objects
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+objects"} monoid objects
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+objects"} group objects
            %p
              are in particular (i.e. have
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} Pointed topological spaces
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+simplicial+sets"} pointed simplicial sets
              are important in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
              (where they are often called
              = succeed ")," do
                %strong based
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fibers"} homotopy fibers
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+objects"} loop space objects
              etc. See also at
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+pointed+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on pointed topological spaces
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+homotopy+types"} pointed homotopy types
          %p
          #PointedCategories.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong (relation to pointed categories)
              %br/
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
              is a “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+category"}> pointed category
              ” in the sense that it contains a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
              (hence a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              which is also
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
              of a pointed object (by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+objects"} initial objects
            %p
              Moreover, any category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
              of pointed objects is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+category"} pointed category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
              being
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mo ∃
                          %mo !
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \overset{\exists !}{\to} \ast
            %p
              Alternatively, it makes (more?) sense to understand under a “pointed category” a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E}, E)
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories"} Categories
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              equipped with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \in \mathcal{E}
              = succeed "-pointed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,x_E)
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{E}, E)
              are morphisms of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi E
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_E \colon E \to X
              (i.e.
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+elements"} generalized elements
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              at stage
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Pointed
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-categories"} n-categories
              figure prominently in the
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+hypothesis"} delooping hypothesis
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/k-tuply+monoidal+n-category"} k-tuply monoidal n-category
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PointedSets"}
              = succeed "." do
                %em 0-tuply monoidal 0-category
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#forgetting_and_adjoining_basepoints Forgetting and adjoining basepoints
          #BasePointAdjoined.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+colimits"} finite colimits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/} \to \mathcal{C}
              from its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+pointed+objects"} category of pointed objects
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfPointedObjects"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              given by forming the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"}> coproduct
              ) with a base point (“adjoining a base point”), this is denoted by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)_+ \coloneqq (-) \sqcup \ast \;\colon \; \mathcal{C} \longrightarrow \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
                    \\,.
          %h3#zero_object_and_pointed_category_structure Zero object and pointed category structure
          #PointedObjectsHaveZeroObject.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+pointed+objects"} category of pointed objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfPointedObjects"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              coincides with the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \in \mathcal{C}
              itself, pointed in the unique way.
            %p
              In this situation one says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
              is a
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
              and that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+category"} pointed category
            %p
              It follows that also all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}(X,Y)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
              are canonically
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+sets"} pointed sets
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+morphism"} zero morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∃
                        %mo !
                    %mn 0
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ∃
                    %mi Y
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X \overset{\exists!}{\longrightarrow} 0 \overset{\exists}{\longrightarrow} Y
                    \\,.
          %p
            Conversely, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+object"} zero object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is equivalent to its category of pointed objects.
          %h3#limits_and_colimits Limits and colimits
          #LimitsAndColimitsOfPointedObjects.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              with all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+pointed+objects"} category of pointed objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CategoryOfPointedObjects"}
            %p Moreover:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the limits are the limits of the underlying diagrams in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %li
                %p
                  the colimits are the colimits in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  of the diagrams
                  = succeed "." do
                    %em with the basepoint adjoined
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              It is immediate to check the relevant
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "overcategory#LimitsAndColimits"} slice category – limits and colimits
          %h3#WedgeSumAndSmashProduct Wedge sum and Smash product
          #WedgeSumAsCoproduct.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              Given two pointed objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,x)
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y,y)
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
                  is simply
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ×
                          %mi Y
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X\times Y, (x,y))
              %li
                %p
                  their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
                  has to be computed using the second clause in prop.
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LimitsAndColimitsOfPointedObjects"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
                  has to be adjoined to the diagram, it is given not by the coproduct in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  of the form:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo *
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mi x
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mi y
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi po
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi Y
                              %mtd
                                %mo ⟶
                              %mtd
                                %mi X
                                %mo ∨
                                %mi Y
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \\ast &amp;\overset{x}{\longrightarrow}&amp; X
                        \\\
                        {}^{\mathllap{y}}\downarrow &amp;(po)&amp; \downarrow
                        \\\
                        Y &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X \vee Y
                        }
                        \\,.
                %p
                  This is called the
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
                  operation on pointed objects.
            %p
              Generally for a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X_i\}_{i \in I}
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{\ast/}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product
                  is formed in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Top
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
              %li
                %p
                  their
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
                  is formed by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Top
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
                  over the diagram with a basepoint adjoined, and is called the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∨
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi I
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee_{i \in I} X_i
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of its
              = succeed "-skeleton" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-skeleton" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wedge+sum"} wedge sum
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#WedgeSumAsCoproduct"}
              = succeed "-spheres," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "-cell" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ≃
                    %munder
                      %mo ∨
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi I
                          %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X^n / X^{n-1} \simeq \underset{i \in I_n}{\vee} S^n
                    \\,.
          #SmashProductOfPointedObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
